  /* ── Scrolling, without ever taking the gesture ───────────────────────────
   *
   * The obvious way to make these views scroll is `overflow-y: auto`. Do not.
   * On iOS Safari a nested scroller CLAIMS the whole touch gesture: when it
   * reaches its end the page does not take over, it stops, and the reader has
